00:07:28,080 --> 00:07:29,280
drag and reduce

310
00:07:29,320 --> 00:07:30,240
the aircraft's flight

311
00:07:30,320 --> 00:07:30,880
performance.

312
00:07:31,280 --> 00:07:32,560
Internal weapons bays

313
00:07:32,640 --> 00:07:33,600
allowed the aircraft

314
00:07:33,680 --> 00:07:34,320
to preserve

315
00:07:34,440 --> 00:07:35,680
its aerodynamic shape.

316
00:07:36,080 --> 00:07:37,200
The rotary launchers

317
00:07:37,400 --> 00:07:38,160
enabled the missiles

318
00:07:38,200 --> 00:07:39,600
to be fired sequentially.

319
00:07:40,080 --> 00:07:41,440
Operating such a machine

320
00:07:41,680 --> 00:07:43,040
required a crew of four.

321
00:07:43,520 --> 00:07:44,720
The cockpit accommodated

322
00:07:44,800 --> 00:07:46,400
the commander, the co-pilot,

323
00:07:46,760 --> 00:07:47,840
and two navigators,

324
00:07:48,240 --> 00:07:49,520
one of whom was responsible

325
00:07:49,600 --> 00:07:50,720
for weapons employment.

326
00:07:51,280 --> 00:07:52,080
Now the sheer

327
00:07:52,320 --> 00:07:54,000
scale of the aircraft began

328
00:07:54,080 --> 00:07:55,200
to make sense.

329
00:07:55,307 --> 00:07:55,680
A single

330
00:07:55,840 --> 00:07:57,440
fuselage had to accommodate

331
00:07:57,600 --> 00:07:58,960
enormous fuel reserves,

332
00:07:59,360 --> 00:08:00,720
four powerful engines,

333
00:08:01,040 --> 00:08:02,720
a complex variable-sweep

334
00:08:02,800 --> 00:08:03,520
wing structure,

335
00:08:04,040 --> 00:08:05,200
equipment for long-distance

336
00:08:05,280 --> 00:08:06,320
flight, and two

337
00:08:06,480 --> 00:08:07,680
weapons bays carrying

338
00:08:07,840 --> 00:08:08,960
heavy missile armament.

339
00:08:09,400 --> 00:08:10,720
And it was these missiles

340
00:08:10,800 --> 00:08:13,280
that defined the Tu-160's role

341
00:08:13,360 --> 00:08:14,320
in the confrontation

342
00:08:14,400 --> 00:08:15,600
with the United States.

343
00:08:16,000 --> 00:08:17,520
The aircraft was not designed

344
00:08:17,560 --> 00:08:18,640
to destroy American

345
00:08:18,720 --> 00:08:20,000
military infrastructure

346
00:08:20,080 --> 00:08:20,960
single-handedly.

347
00:08:21,400 --> 00:08:22,000
Its purpose

348
00:08:22,080 --> 00:08:22,880
was to complement

349
00:08:22,960 --> 00:08:23,680
land-based

350
00:08:23,760 --> 00:08:24,880
and submarine-launched

351
00:08:24,960 --> 00:08:26,720
ballistic missiles by providing

352
00:08:26,800 --> 00:08:28,240
another means of delivering

353
00:08:28,320 --> 00:08:29,280
nuclear weapons.

354
00:08:29,680 --> 00:08:31,200
However, the Tu-160

355
00:08:31,440 --> 00:08:33,280
was not invulnerable.

356
00:08:33,600 --> 00:08:35,280
American fighter aircraft,

357
00:08:35,640 --> 00:08:36,800
radar installations,

358
00:08:37,000 --> 00:08:38,320
and air defense systems

359
00:08:38,400 --> 00:08:40,000
remained serious threats.

360
00:08:40,320 --> 00:08:41,760
The aircraft also depended

361
00:08:41,840 --> 00:08:42,720
on airfields,

362
00:08:43,000 --> 00:08:44,000
logistical support,

363
00:08:44,280 --> 00:08:45,360
and communications.

364
00:08:45,760 --> 00:08:46,480
Nevertheless,

365
00:08:46,720 --> 00:08:47,520
the introduction

366
00:08:47,600 --> 00:08:48,880
of such a missile carrier

367
00:08:49,200 --> 00:08:50,400
expanded the capabilities

368
00:08:50,480 --> 00:08:52,160
of Soviet strategic forces.

369
00:08:52,520 --> 00:08:53,520
The United States

370
00:08:53,600 --> 00:08:54,560
now had to account

371
00:08:54,640 --> 00:08:56,160
for another type of nuclear

372
00:08:56,240 --> 00:08:57,520
weapons delivery system.

373
00:08:58,000 --> 00:08:59,600
By the early 1980s,

374
00:08:59,840 --> 00:09:00,720
the main elements

375
00:09:00,760 --> 00:09:02,800
of the Tu-160's design

376
00:09:02,880 --> 00:09:03,920
had been brought together

377
00:09:04,000 --> 00:09:05,520
in a prototype aircraft.

378
00:09:05,840 --> 00:09:07,360
On the ground, engineers

379
00:09:07,440 --> 00:09:08,480
could test the engines,

380
00:09:08,800 --> 00:09:09,680
wing mechanisms,

381
00:09:10,040 --> 00:09:11,440
control systems, and other

382
00:09:11,520 --> 00:09:12,640
components separately.

383
00:09:13,000 --> 00:09:14,080
But only flight

384
00:09:14,160 --> 00:09:15,120
could demonstrate how

385
00:09:15,200 --> 00:09:16,560
this entire complex

386
00:09:16,800 --> 00:09:17,680
structure would work

387
00:09:17,720 --> 00:09:18,960
as a single machine.

388
00:09:19,320 --> 00:09:20,480
On December eighteenth,

389
00:09:20,680 --> 00:09:21,600
nineteen eighty-one,

390
00:09:22,000 --> 00:09:24,240
the prototype Tu-160 took

391
00:09:24,320 --> 00:09:25,920
to the air for the first time.

392
00:09:26,360 --> 00:09:27,360
Test pilot Boris

393
00:09:27,440 --> 00:09:29,040
Veremey was at the controls.

394
00:09:29,440 --> 00:09:30,880
That flight opened a new

395
00:09:31,040 --> 00:09:32,160
phase of the program.

396
00:09:32,480 --> 00:09:34,080
Engineers now had to study

397
00:09:34,160 --> 00:09:35,440
the aircraft's behavior

398
00:09:35,520 --> 00:09:36,960
in the air, gradually

399
00:09:37,040 --> 00:09:38,240
testing its performance

400
00:09:38,320 --> 00:09:39,520
and onboard equipment.

401
00:09:40,200 --> 00:09:41,440
Meanwhile, preparations

402
00:09:41,560 --> 00:09:42,560
for serial production

403
00:09:42,640 --> 00:09:44,160
were underway in Kazan.

404
00:09:44,560 --> 00:09:46,880
Building the Tu-160 required

405
00:09:47,080 --> 00:09:48,320
mastering the manufacture

406
00:09:48,400 --> 00:09:49,920
of large and complex

407
00:09:50,160 --> 00:09:51,040
structural components,

408
00:09:51,360 --> 00:09:52,560
organizing the assembly

409
00:09:52,640 --> 00:09:53,440
of an enormous

410
00:09:53,520 --> 00:09:55,280
airframe, and coordinating

411
00:09:55,360 --> 00:09:56,480
the different factories

412
00:09:56,600 --> 00:09:57,920
responsible for producing

413
00:09:58,000 --> 00:09:59,360
the aircraft's individual

414
00:09:59,440 --> 00:09:59,920
systems.

415
00:10:00,320 --> 00:10:01,680
In 1984,

416
00:10:01,760 --> 00:10:03,200
testing began on the first

417
00:10:03,280 --> 00:10:05,360
production Tu-160.

418
00:10:05,467 --> 00:10:07,440
And in April 1987,

419
00:10:07,547 --> 00:10:08,160
the new missile

420
00:10:08,280 --> 00:10:09,600
carriers began entering

421
00:10:09,800 --> 00:10:11,120
service with an operational

422
00:10:11,200 --> 00:10:12,800
long-range aviation unit

423
00:10:12,880 --> 00:10:14,640
in Pryluky, in what was then

424
00:10:14,680 --> 00:10:16,000
the Ukrainian Soviet

425
00:10:16,160 --> 00:10:17,360
Socialist Republic.

426
00:10:17,520 --> 00:10:18,560
More than ten years

427
00:10:18,640 --> 00:10:19,120
had passed

428
00:10:19,200 --> 00:10:20,000
between the beginning

429
00:10:20,080 --> 00:10:21,600
of the aircraft's development

430
00:10:21,680 --> 00:10:22,480
and its arrival

431
00:10:22,560 --> 00:10:24,000
in military service.

432
00:10:24,160 --> 00:10:25,920
The Tu-160 acquired

433
00:10:26,000 --> 00:10:27,600
an unofficial nickname:

434
00:10:27,680 --> 00:10:29,120
the White Swan.

435
00:10:29,227 --> 00:10:31,280
Its enormous white fuselage,

436
00:10:31,360 --> 00:10:33,120
long pointed nose, four

437
00:10:33,200 --> 00:10:34,480
engines beneath the central

438
00:10:34,560 --> 00:10:35,440
wing section,

439
00:10:35,600 --> 00:10:36,800
and movable wings gave

440
00:10:36,880 --> 00:10:38,640
it an unusual silhouette.

441
00:10:38,720 --> 00:10:39,960
On the ground, it looked

442
00:10:40,000 --> 00:10:41,520
like a gigantic machine

443
00:10:41,600 --> 00:10:43,520
with its wings spread wide.

444
00:10:43,600 --> 00:10:45,040
During high-speed flight,

445
00:10:45,120 --> 00:10:46,400
the wings swept farther

446
00:10:46,720 --> 00:10:47,760
backward, transforming

447
00:10:47,840 --> 00:10:49,200
the aircraft's entire

448
00:10:49,280 --> 00:10:50,160
appearance.

449
00:10:50,280 --> 00:10:51,600
NATO gave it the reporting

450
00:10:51,680 --> 00:10:53,200
name Blackjack.

451
00:10:53,307 --> 00:10:54,880
But shortly after the Tu-160

452
00:10:55,120 --> 00:10:57,280
entered operational service,

453
00:10:57,387 --> 00:10:58,560
the country it had been built

454
00:10:58,640 --> 00:11:00,480
for ceased to exist.

455
00:11:00,533 --> 00:11:02,560
In December 1991,

456
00:11:02,640 --> 00:11:04,880
the Soviet Union collapsed.

457
00:11:04,960 --> 00:11:05,840
Some of the missile

458
00:11:06,000 --> 00:11:07,440
carriers that had been built

459
00:11:07,520 --> 00:11:08,880
remained in independent

460
00:11:08,960 --> 00:11:10,560
Ukraine, while others

461
00:11:10,640 --> 00:11:11,840
were located in Russia.

462
00:11:12,400 --> 00:11:13,600
In the following years,

463
00:11:13,840 --> 00:11:14,880
some of the Ukrainian

464
00:11:15,000 --> 00:11:16,240
aircraft were destroyed

465
00:11:16,320 --> 00:11:17,440
as part of disarmament

466
00:11:17,520 --> 00:11:18,960
programs, while eight

467
00:11:19,120 --> 00:11:20,320
were transferred to Russia.

468
00:11:21,120 --> 00:11:22,320
Production of the Tu-160

469
00:11:22,480 --> 00:11:24,720
almost completely stopped.

470
00:11:25,200 --> 00:11:26,560
But the surviving aircraft

471
00:11:26,640 --> 00:11:27,760
remained in service.

472
00:11:28,320 --> 00:11:29,600
Later, Russia began

473
00:11:29,680 --> 00:11:30,560
modernizing them,

474
00:11:30,840 --> 00:11:31,600
and eventually

475
00:11:31,760 --> 00:11:32,720
resumed the production

476
00:11:32,760 --> 00:11:33,760
of new aircraft.

477
00:11:34,320 --> 00:11:36,080
In January 2022,

478
00:11:36,400 --> 00:11:39,280
a newly built Tu-160M took

479
00:11:39,360 --> 00:11:40,960
to the air for the first time.

480
00:11:41,440 --> 00:11:42,640
This was not an older

481
00:11:42,760 --> 00:11:44,000
aircraft that had undergone

482
00:11:44,080 --> 00:11:44,880
modernization,

483
00:11:45,200 --> 00:11:46,720
but a newly manufactured

484
00:11:46,800 --> 00:11:47,600
missile carrier.

485
00:11:48,160 --> 00:11:48,800
By that point,

486
00:11:49,200 --> 00:11:50,560
forty years had passed

487
00:11:50,640 --> 00:11:51,600
since the prototype

488
00:11:51,680 --> 00:11:53,680
Tu-160's first flight.

489
00:11:54,160 --> 00:11:55,760
The Cold War had ended.

490
00:11:56,160 --> 00:11:57,280
The Soviet Union

491
00:11:57,520 --> 00:11:58,640
no longer existed.

492
00:11:59,040 --> 00:12:00,240
But the aircraft built

493
00:12:00,320 --> 00:12:01,840
for a nuclear confrontation

494
00:12:01,920 --> 00:12:02,560
with the United

495
00:12:02,640 --> 00:12:04,160
States had outlived

496
00:12:04,240 --> 00:12:05,760
the country that created it.
